In JavaScript, isAdmin('0') returns true but should be false. Fix it:
```js
function isAdmin(role) {
  return role == 0;
}
```

loadUser returns a Promise instead of the user's name. Fix it:
```js
async function loadUser(id) {
  const res = fetchUser(id);
  return res.name;
}
```

average([1, 2]) returns 1 instead of 1.5 in this Python 3 code. Fix it:
```python
def average(xs):
    return sum(xs) // len(xs)
```

sortDesc should sort numbers from largest to smallest but sorts them as strings ascending:
```js
function sortDesc(nums) {
  return nums.sort();
}
```

count_lines leaves the file open. Fix it without changing behavior:
```python
def count_lines(path):
    f = open(path)
    return len(f.readlines())
```

inRange(10, 1, 10) returns false but the upper bound should be inclusive:
```ts
function inRange(x: number, lo: number, hi: number): boolean {
  return x >= lo && x < hi;
}
```
